e county&rsquo;s 6 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and August to September came in under 90% of normal in 33 of those 75 years. In 2025 that same pair came in at 47% of normal on the middle, while April to May hit 135%. So far in 2026, May to June sits at 147% of normal on the middle. Grid 23881 had its driest year in 1960 at 65% of normal.</p>"}
